<%
# ============================================================================
# MISSION 4: CRITICAL FAILURE - SCENARIO FILE
# ============================================================================
# Break Escape - Season 1: The Architect's Shadow
#
# Grid-scale battery energy storage attack. ENTROPY's Critical Mass cell has
# infiltrated the Albion Energy Storage facility (200 MWh lithium-ion BESS) and
# compromised the BMS/SCADA to falsify thermal sensors and disable the hydrogen
# venting and Emergency Shutdown (ESD) interlocks — driving the battery racks
# toward catastrophic thermal runaway. At 0800 the racks tip into a chain fire /
# hydrogen explosion, taking the grid down for 240,000 people and levelling the
# site. Cross-cell coordination with Social Fabric revealed.
#
# Setting/assets adapted from sis02_energy (battery hall, SCADA control room,
# rack status panels, H2 detector, analog thermometer, ESD pushbutton).
#
# ENTROPY Cell: Critical Mass
# Mission Type: Infrastructure Crisis / Tactical Response
# Difficulty: Intermediate (Mission 4)
#
# NEW MECHANICS:
# - Combat encounters with hostile NPCs
# - Stage-based urgency system (no timer)
# - SCADA / BMS investigation (falsified telemetry vs physical instrument)
# - Multi-vector attack disabling + Emergency Shutdown (ESD) minigame
# - Critical tactical choices
#
# ROOM LAYOUT (PASS 3 puzzle chains -- see PUZZLE_CHAINS_PLAN.md):
#
#   main_entrance (guard)
#     +-- S -> operations_office (Vance: Level 1 card is CLONED off him -- m03 cloner)
#                +-- S -> security_office            locker [key] spare Level 1; reader export (clue)
#                +-- E -> scada_control_room
#                           +-- E -> battery_hall_1 (Cipher, optional; Duty Round Panel = Vance's print)
#                                      +-- S -> engineering_workshop  [rfid: Level 2]  VM, flag station,
#                                      |                              OptiGrid tool case [key] -> fingerprint kit
#                                      +-- E -> battery_hall_2 / inverter room  [rfid: Level 1]  (Relay: drops Level 2)
#                                                 +-- S -> plant_room  [biometric: Robert Vance]  (Voltage + Static, ESD)
#                                                            +-- E -> loading_dock  (go-bag [key]); Voltage's escape route
#
# Chain: the plant reader is met in Hall 2 before the workshop can open (its card is
# Relay's), the kit is in the workshop, and the print is on the way back through Hall 1.
#
# Layout reworked 2026-08-21 (ALIGNMENT_PLAN Phase 1b) to clear four world-space
# overlaps. Two structural changes, both of which also tightened the lock chain:
#   * engineering_workshop had a SECOND door from scada_control_room that bypassed
#     Cipher entirely; it now hangs only off battery_hall_1.
#   * plant_room hung off battery_hall_1, so it sat next to the hall before the
#     player had ever met Relay; it now hangs off battery_hall_2, which is what
#     makes the Master keycard a genuine gate.
# Verify with: ruby scripts/validate_scenario.rb (world-space overlap check).
#
# PASS 2 (playtest D1): scada -> battery_hall_1 was a SOUTH connection, and the
# doorway opened onto the hall's solid north wall. The engine placed the 20-wide
# hall under the 10-wide control room using the parity of the control room's
# ORIGIN (rooms.js positionSouthSingle), but placed each door by the parity of
# the SHARED WALL (doors.js placeSouthDoorSingle / placeNorthDoorSingle).
# room_control_1x2gu is 10x6, a stacking height of 1 grid unit (odd), so the two
# parities disagree and the doors land 320px apart. The validator checks overlap,
# not door alignment. The hall now hangs EAST of the control room: E/W pairs are
# top-aligned and both doors sit at top + 2.5 tiles, so they always line up.
# Every connection was re-checked against a port of the engine's BFS and door
# placement (all aligned, no overlaps).
# ============================================================================

# ERB Helper Methods
require 'base64'

def base64_encode(text)
  Base64.strict_encode64(text)
end

# Narrative Content Variables
vance_warning_email = "From: Robert Vance\nTo: OT Security\nDate: 12 January\nSubject: Unscheduled Maintenance Crew\n\nTeam,\n\nOptiGrid Solutions sent a maintenance crew on Thursday night (not on our schedule). They had proper RFID credentials but I have no work order on file. They were in the BMS cabinet and the SCADA control room for over three hours.\n\nCan someone verify their authorisation before I escalate?\n\n-Robert"

voltage_attack_note = "CRITICAL MASS OPERATION LOG\n\nPhase 2 complete. BMS interlock-bypass modules installed on rack banks A, B and C.\nThermal sensors falsified at the SCADA layer. Hydrogen venting and ESD interlocks disabled.\nRemote overcharge trigger armed.\n\nCoordination with Social Fabric confirmed - simultaneous infrastructure strikes across the region.\n\nTrigger scheduled: 0800 local. The racks tip into thermal runaway. Grid drops for 240,000. The hall goes up with it.\nFail-safe disabled. No automatic shutdown.\n\nThe Architect sends regards. Phase 3 begins after successful execution.\n\n- Voltage"

%>
{
  "scenario_brief": "Infiltrate the Albion Energy Storage facility — 200 MWh of grid-scale lithium-ion battery storage — to investigate a suspected ENTROPY operation. The Critical Mass cell has weaponised the BMS and SCADA systems to drive the battery racks into thermal runaway, threatening a catastrophic fire and a grid blackout for 240,000 people. Confirm the falsified telemetry against a real instrument and prove how they took control: the Emergency Shutdown arms only once grid control has both. Keep the trigger holder away from his laptop, then press the shutdown before the 0800 trigger time.",

  "show_scenario_brief": "once",

  <%# Pass 5 alignment A2 (m03 P1-31 pattern): one condition per story phase, so a
      reload (game_loaded) and the end of a fight (all_hostiles_ko) return to the
      phase's own playlist instead of the opening noir. The four are mutually
      exclusive once the briefing has played. clock_started is set when the attack
      is mapped or when Vance sounds the evacuation, whichever comes first (see
      timers); the hydrogen alarm implies it. %>
  <%
    music_clockish = "(globalVars.clock_started === true || globalVars.hydrogen_alarm === true)"
    music_day      = "globalVars.briefing_played === true && globalVars.anomaly_detected !== true && !#{music_clockish} && globalVars.attack_prevented !== true"
    music_threat   = "globalVars.briefing_played === true && globalVars.anomaly_detected === true && !#{music_clockish} && globalVars.attack_prevented !== true"
    music_clock    = "globalVars.briefing_played === true && #{music_clockish} && globalVars.attack_prevented !== true"
    music_after    = "globalVars.briefing_played === true && globalVars.attack_prevented === true"
  %>
  "music": {
    "events": [
      {
        "trigger": "game_loaded",
        "condition": "!globalVars.briefing_played",
        "playlist": "cutscene",
        "fade": false
      },
      { "trigger": "game_loaded", "condition": "<%= music_day %>",    "playlist": "noir",       "fade": false },
      { "trigger": "game_loaded", "condition": "<%= music_threat %>", "playlist": "threat",     "fade": false },
      { "trigger": "game_loaded", "condition": "<%= music_clock %>",  "playlist": "spy-action", "fade": false },
      { "trigger": "game_loaded", "condition": "<%= music_after %>",  "playlist": "end",        "fade": false },
      {
        "trigger": "conversation_closed:opening_briefing_cutscene",
        "playlist": "noir",
        "fade": true
      },
      {
        "comment": "The telemetry is confirmed false -- the mission turns here. Not when the clock is already running (a dial read late, after the flags).",
        "trigger": "global_variable_changed:anomaly_detected",
        "condition": "value === true && !<%= music_clockish %> && globalVars.attack_prevented !== true",
        "playlist": "threat",
        "fade": true
      },
      {
        "comment": "The clock starts: the attack is mapped, or the evacuation alarm has told Voltage he's been found.",
        "trigger": "global_variable_changed:clock_started",
        "condition": "value === true && globalVars.attack_prevented !== true",
        "playlist": "spy-action",
        "fade": true
      },
      {
        "comment": "Hydrogen advisory: bank B is venting. Escalate and stay escalated until the shutdown.",
        "trigger": "global_variable_changed:hydrogen_alarm",
        "condition": "value === true && globalVars.attack_prevented !== true",
        "playlist": "spy-action",
        "fade": true
      },
      <%# Round 2 (browser N1, review m13): a fight plays threat before the clock
          and keeps spy-action once the clock runs; nothing after the shutdown.
          A reload restores hostile NPCs with {restored: true} (npc-hostile.js:107),
          which must not change the phase's music. typeof keeps the condition safe
          when the key is absent. %>
      {
        "trigger": "npc_hostile_state_changed",
        "condition": "isHostile === true && (typeof restored === 'undefined' || !restored) && !<%= music_clockish %> && globalVars.attack_prevented !== true",
        "playlist": "threat",
        "fade": true
      },
      {
        "trigger": "npc_hostile_state_changed",
        "condition": "isHostile === true && (typeof restored === 'undefined' || !restored) && <%= music_clockish %> && globalVars.attack_prevented !== true",
        "playlist": "spy-action",
        "fade": true
      },
      { "trigger": "all_hostiles_ko", "condition": "<%= music_day %>",    "playlist": "noir",       "fade": true },
      { "trigger": "all_hostiles_ko", "condition": "<%= music_threat %>", "playlist": "threat",     "fade": true },
      { "trigger": "all_hostiles_ko", "condition": "<%= music_clock %>",  "playlist": "spy-action", "fade": true },
      { "trigger": "all_hostiles_ko", "condition": "<%= music_after %>",  "playlist": "end",        "fade": true },
      {
        "comment": "A4: the shutdown is in and the sweep begins under a settled cue. The credits follow the debrief.",
        "trigger": "global_variable_changed:attack_prevented",
        "condition": "value === true",
        "playlist": "end",
        "fade": true
      },
      {
        "trigger": "conversation_closed:agent_0x99_debrief",
        "playlist": "victory",
        "track": "Safetynet in the Smoke",
        "autoStop": true,
        "disableClose": true,
        "fade": true,
        "credits": [
          { "text": "MISSION COMPLETE", "style": "title", "condition": "globalVars.attack_prevented && !globalVars.racks_vented" },
          { "text": "COSTLY SUCCESS", "style": "title", "condition": "globalVars.attack_prevented && globalVars.racks_vented" },
          <%# Struggling run A (F3): the mission name read as a second headline beside
              COSTLY SUCCESS. Exactly one headline (the title); the subtitle names the mission. %>
          { "text": "MISSION 4: CRITICAL FAILURE", "style": "subtitle" },
          { "text": "" },
          { "text": "ALBION ENERGY STORAGE: THERMAL RUNAWAY AVERTED — Emergency Shutdown engaged", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.attack_prevented && !globalVars.racks_vented" },
          { "text": "GRID HELD: 240,000 residents kept on supply", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.attack_prevented && !globalVars.racks_vented" },
          <%# Pass 5 decision 1: eleven on site = the nine night crew, Vance and the
              gate guard. "Walked out" only when the crew got out (or never needed
              to) and nobody was carried. crew_lost is set when a bank vents with
              the crew still in Hall 2. %>
          { "text": "ALL ELEVEN ON SITE WALKED OUT", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.attack_prevented && !globalVars.crew_lost && !globalVars.security_guard_ko && !globalVars.robert_vance_ko" },
          { "text": "EVERYONE ON SITE GOT OUT ALIVE — not all of them on their own feet", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.attack_prevented && !globalVars.crew_lost && (globalVars.security_guard_ko || globalVars.robert_vance_ko)" },
          { "text": "NIGHT CREW: out of Hall 2 on Vance's alarm, and the cell heard it too", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.crew_warned" },
          { "text": "RACK BANK B LOST — banks A and C isolated in time", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.racks_vented && !globalVars.vented_by_trigger" },
          { "text": "RACK BANK B LOST — he reached the laptop before you put him down", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.vented_by_trigger" },
          { "text": "CASUALTIES: the Hall 2 night crew, and the dropped feed", "style": "warning", "condition": "globalVars.crew_lost" },
          { "text": "CASUALTIES: two on the dropped feed. Hall 2 was empty when it went", "style": "warning", "condition": "globalVars.casualties_occurred && !globalVars.crew_lost" },
          { "text": "" },
          { "text": "── DECISIONS ──", "style": "section-header" },
          { "text": "VOLTAGE: CAPTURED — Blackout's field lead in custody", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.voltage_captured" },
          { "text": "VOLTAGE: ESCAPED — you took the button and let him reach the dock", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.voltage_escaped" },
          { "text": "ROBERT VANCE: brought in — ran the desk while you ran the halls", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.vance_is_ally" },
          { "text": "ROBERT VANCE: never told — the cover held all night", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.vance_spoken && !globalVars.vance_is_ally && !globalVars.robert_vance_ko" },
          { "text": "ROBERT VANCE: never met — you went round him", "style": "entry", "condition": "!globalVars.vance_spoken && !globalVars.vance_is_ally && !globalVars.robert_vance_ko" },
          { "text": "ROBERT VANCE: knocked down in his own office, by us", "style": "warning", "condition": "globalVars.robert_vance_ko" },
          { "text": "GATE GUARD: knocked out at his own desk, doing his job by the book", "style": "warning", "condition": "globalVars.security_guard_ko" },
          { "text": "CIPHER: walked off the job when you told him about the night crew", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.cipher_walked" },
          { "text": "STATIC: stood aside, and left with Voltage", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.static_left && !globalVars.static_left_alone" },
          { "text": "STATIC: stood aside, and slipped out when Voltage fell", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.static_left_alone" },
          { "text": "RELAY: card copied mid-standoff", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.relay_card_cloned" },
          <%# Puzzle chains R3-3: the optional break-in documents get a word at the end. %>
          { "text": "THE BREAK-IN: traced on paper to the OptiGrid crew", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.evidence_maintenance_logs_found || globalVars.evidence_camera_tampering_found || globalVars.evidence_reader_spoof_found || globalVars.evidence_access_logs_found" },
          { "text": "EVIDENCE: Voltage's own print on the bypass module", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.voltage_print_on_bypass" },
          { "text": "SOCIAL FABRIC SAFEHOUSE: located", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.lore_safehouse_address_found" },
          <%# Struggling run A (F3 sweep): the credits match the debrief's crew-lost lines. %>
          { "text": "DISCLOSED IN FULL — the attack, the vulnerabilities, and how close it came", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.disclosure_choice === 'full' && !globalVars.crew_lost" },
          { "text": "DISCLOSED IN FULL — the attack, the vulnerabilities, and the nine it cost", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.disclosure_choice === 'full' && globalVars.crew_lost" },
          { "text": "CLASSIFIED — filed as a maintenance fault, patched quietly", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.disclosure_choice === 'quiet' && !globalVars.crew_lost" },
          { "text": "CLASSIFIED — filed as an industrial accident, cause under investigation", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.disclosure_choice === 'quiet' && globalVars.crew_lost" },
          { "text": "PARTIALLY DISCLOSED — an incident acknowledged, the details withheld", "style": "entry", "condition": "globalVars.disclosure_choice === 'partial'" },
          { "text": "" },
          { "text": "BLACKOUT: signed the casualty model. Still at large.", "style": "warning", "condition": "globalVars.blackout_named" },
          { "text": "THE ARCHITECT: identity still unknown. Phase 3 looms.", "style": "warning" },
          { "text": "ENTROPY: Still operational. Cross-cell strikes continue.", "style": "warning" }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },

  "narrator": {
    "id": "narrator",
    "skipTextValidation": true,
    "voice": {
      "name": "Algenib",
      "style": "Cinematic noir detective voice over narrator.",
      "language": "en-GB"
    }
  },

  "objectives": [
    {
      "aimId": "get_inside",
      "title": "Get Inside Albion Energy Storage",
      "description": "Talk your way past the checkpoint and find someone on shift who knows the plant",
      "status": "active",
      "order": 0,
      "tasks": [
        {
          "taskId": "enter_facility",
          "title": "Get past the checkpoint into the operations office",
          "type": "enter_room",
          "targetRoom": "operations_office",
          "status": "active"
        },
        {
          <%# Browser M-2: optional, so a player who gets in without him isn't left
              with an open task (the hub already treats the step as done). %>
          "taskId": "meet_robert_vance",
          "title": "Find the OT engineer on shift",
          "type": "npc_conversation",
          "targetNPC": "robert_vance",
          "status": "active",
          "optional": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "aimId": "confirm_the_lie",
      "title": "Confirm the Telemetry Is Lying",
      "description": "The control room says the racks are nominal. Find out whether that is true",
      "status": "locked",
      "unlockCondition": { "aimCompleted": "get_inside" },
      "order": 1,
      "tasks": [
        <%# Puzzle chains R2-1: optional. The paper evidence gates nothing since the
            gate was retired (see the flag-tracking comment on agent_0x99). What it
            still earns: this task's tick and score, the work-order HaX text, the
            work-order route to dropping the cover with Vance, the reader export's
            print clue, and (R3-3) a credits line. The debrief doesn't read it. The
            objectives panel draws an optional task like a required one. The aim
            completes on the dial. %>
        {
          "taskId": "find_infiltration_evidence",
          <%# Scenario design m11: retitled "(Optional) …" as a stopgap, then the
              prefix was dropped (a0d7a195) once the objectives panel marked required
              tasks with * and dimmed optional ones (engine 9290f89f). %>
          "title": "Find evidence of the break-in",
          "type": "custom",
          "status": "active",
          "optional": true
        },
        {
          "taskId": "identify_scada_anomalies",
          "title": "Verify the rack temperatures independently",
          "type": "custom",
          "status": "active"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "aimId": "reach_the_workshop",
      "title": "Reach the Engineering Workshop",
      "description": "The workshop is the only place with a route onto the OT network — and it is behind a card you do not have",
      "status": "locked",
      "unlockCondition": { "aimCompleted": "confirm_the_lie" },
      "order": 2,
      "tasks": [
        {
          "taskId": "neutralize_operative_relay",
          "title": "Take a workshop card off the cell",
          "type": "custom",
          "status": "active"
        },
        {
          "taskId": "locate_compromised_systems",
          "title": "Get into the engineering workshop",
          "type": "enter_room",
          "targetRoom": "engineering_workshop",
          "status": "active"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "aimId": "map_the_attack",
      "title": "Map the Attack on the OT Network",
      "description": "Work the BMS jump server from the workshop terminal and prove how they took control",
      "status": "locked",
      "unlockCondition": { "aimCompleted": "reach_the_workshop" },
      "order": 3,
      "tasks": [
        {
          "taskId": "scan_scada_network",
          "title": "Map the OT network",
          "type": "custom",
          "status": "active",
          "optional": true
        },
        {
          "taskId": "submit_network_scan_flag",
          "title": "Submit the flag from the fake rack status page",
          "type": "submit_flags",
          "targetFlags": ["flag_station_dropsite:bms_jump_server-flag1"],
          "targetCount": 1,
          "currentCount": 0,
          "showProgress": true,
          "status": "active"
        },
        {
          "taskId": "investigate_compromised_services",
          "title": "Enumerate what is listening",
          "type": "custom",
          "status": "active",
          "optional": true
        },
        {
          "taskId": "submit_ftp_intel_flag",
          "title": "Submit the intelligence file from their FTP service",
          "type": "submit_flags",
          "targetFlags": ["flag_station_dropsite:bms_jump_server-flag2"],
          "targetCount": 1,
          "currentCount": 0,
          "showProgress": true,
          "status": "active"
        },
        {
          "taskId": "exploit_distcc_vulnerability",
          "title": "Get a foothold on the BMS jump server",
          "type": "custom",
          "status": "active",
          "optional": true
        },
        {
          "taskId": "submit_distcc_exploit_flag",
          "title": "Submit proof of the distcc foothold",
          "type": "submit_flags",
          "targetFlags": ["flag_station_dropsite:bms_jump_server-flag4"],
          "targetCount": 1,
          "currentCount": 0,
          "showProgress": true,
          "status": "active"
        },
        {
          "taskId": "submit_privesc_flag",
          "title": "Submit proof you became root on the jump server",
          "type": "submit_flags",
          "targetFlags": ["flag_station_dropsite:bms_jump_server-flag3"],
          "targetCount": 1,
          "currentCount": 0,
          "showProgress": true,
          "status": "active"
        }
      ]
    },
    <%# PASS 2 (playtest D5), updated PASS 3. Voltage can be dealt with before any
        flag is in: Hall 2 opens on the cloned Level 1 card, and the plant room
        behind it opens on Vance's print, which can be taken before the VM. (Relay
        now carries the workshop card, so her task lives in reach_the_workshop.) The engine auto-reveals a locked
        aim the moment any of its tasks completes (objectives-manager.js:414-419,
        573-578), so while these two tasks lived in stop_the_runaway, KO'ing Relay
        early put "Stop the Thermal Runaway" on screen before the attack was even
        mapped. They now have their own aim, revealed at the start of act two.
        stop_the_runaway keeps only tasks that cannot complete before
        map_the_attack (the ESD needs attack_mechanism_known; the debrief needs
        the ESD), so its unlockCondition now holds in practice. %>
    {
      "aimId": "take_back_the_plant",
      "title": "Take the Plant Back from the Cell",
      "description": "The man holding the trigger is in the plant room, off Battery Hall 2",
      "status": "locked",
      "unlockCondition": { "aimCompleted": "confirm_the_lie" },
      "order": 4,
      "tasks": [
        {
          "taskId": "neutralize_operative_cipher",
          "title": "Deal with the intruder in Battery Hall 1",
          "type": "custom",
          "status": "active",
          "optional": true
        },
        {
          "taskId": "get_past_plant_reader",
          "title": "Get into the plant room",
          "type": "enter_room",
          "targetRoom": "plant_room",
          "status": "active"
        },
        {
          "taskId": "confront_voltage",
          "title": "Confront Voltage in the plant room",
          "type": "custom",
          "status": "active"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "aimId": "stop_the_runaway",
      "title": "Stop the Thermal Runaway",
      "description": "The mechanism is proven and the clock is running. Get to the hardwired shutdown",
      "status": "locked",
      "unlockCondition": { "aimCompleted": "map_the_attack" },
      "order": 5,
      "missionConclusion": true,
      <%# Ending gate: the mandatory flag nodes from the dungeon graph -- the
          technical work this mission is not allowed to skip. Story tasks are
          not listed: they cost score if unfinished, they never withhold the
          ending. See README_scenario_design.md#concluderequires. %>
      "concludeRequires": {
        "tasksCompleted": [
          "submit_network_scan_flag",
          "submit_ftp_intel_flag",
          "submit_privesc_flag",
          "submit_distcc_exploit_flag"
        ]
      },
      "conclusionScreen": { "type": "bond_visualiser" },
      "tasks": [
        {
          "taskId": "disable_attack_vectors",
          "title": "Force the shutdown before the racks go",
          "type": "custom",
          "status": "active"
        },
        <%# Pass 5 A4 (m03 call_in_after_sweep pattern): the ESD no longer opens the
            debrief. It sets attack_prevented; HaX's mapping unlocks this task and
            texts "sweep, then call me"; the phone hub's "Bring me in" (extract_go)
            completes it and sets mission_complete, which opens the debrief.
            Optional, as in m03, so a missed unlock can never hold the aim. %>
        {
          "taskId": "call_in_after_sweep",
          "title": "Sweep the site, then call HaX to bring you in",
          "description": "The banks are isolated. Anything you haven't read is still in the plant room and at the dock. When you're ready to leave, call HaX.",
          "type": "custom",
          "status": "locked",
          "optional": true
        },
        {
          "taskId": "report_to_0x99",
          "title": "Report the outcome to SAFETYNET",
          "type": "npc_conversation",
          "targetNPC": "agent_0x99_debrief",
          "status": "active"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],

  <%# Fix pass 2026-10-17 (engine regression F4): phone timestamps showed the real
      wall clock (7:23 ... 8:29, so "it's set for 0800" was sent at 8:29). The night
      is 12 Jan (the plant reader log: Vance's card in at 03:35, a print match at
