  "timers": [
<%# Thermal-runaway clock. Modelled on sis02_energy/scenario.json.erb:387-450, which is
    the worked example for this engine feature (ScenarioTimerDispatcher + ScenarioTimerUI).

    M2: both timers start on attack_mechanism_known -- the moment the player has
    proved how the attack works (all four OT-network flags in) -- NOT on
    anomaly_detected. Starting on anomaly_detected meant both clocks ran on
    wall-time through the whole VM stage, so COSTLY SUCCESS was effectively the
    default outcome. The countdown is now the final act: mechanism proven -> race
    to the plant room and the hardwired ESD. Cancelled by the shutdown
    (attack_prevented). Reload: the dispatcher resumes each started timer from
    its saved running time (scenario-timer-dispatcher.js, exportState and the
    constructor's savedStarted), so a reload neither restarts nor skips a clock.

    Pass 5 round 2 (orchestrator decision 1, review M1 option b): the normal
    pair starts on attack_mechanism_known, as before round 1. An EARLY
    evacuation alarm (before the attack is mapped) sets crew_warned_early, which
    starts a second, longer pair (h2_advisory_alarm 24 min, racks_vent_alarm
    30 min). Both pairs can run; whichever fires first wins (each checks
    racks_vented / hydrogen_alarm, and attack_prevented cancels all four). A late
    alarm starts nothing. With the crew out, a vent costs the bank and the feed,
    not the crew (crew_lost is set only for a vent with the crew still in Hall 2).
    HUD (round 4, review M1 / browser B1): the widget shows the first pending
    showCountdown timer in array order and re-evaluates its condition each tick.
    h2_advisory_alarm's condition includes !attack_mechanism_known, so once the
    attack is mapped the HUD falls through to h2_advisory, the real next event,
    and the alarm's advisory never fires. racks_vent_alarm keeps no such guard,
    so the vent still comes at min(alarm + 30, mapping + 14). If mapping comes
    16+ minutes after the alarm the advisory now lands later than the alarm's
    would have; the HUD never shows a figure later than the real advisory.

    DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE FROM sis02: its h2_evacuation timer fires a
    `show_end_screen` action with outcome "failure" and a "Return to Missions" button,
    which ends the run. m04 must NOT do that. Failure here is avoidable and
    player-caused, but the mission still reaches an ending: the second timer sets
    racks_vented / casualties_occurred and play continues to the debrief and the
    bond_visualiser. See ALIGNMENT_PLAN.md "Decisions taken" #10.

    m04's consequences are larger than sis02's single-facility evacuation: 240,000 on
    the grid, the night crew in Hall 2, and the dropped feed. %>
<%# PASS 3 P11b: the trigger race. FIRST in this array on purpose: the HUD shows
    the first pending showCountdown timer in array order (scenario-timer.js:122-156),
    so placed after h2_advisory it would be hidden. A player KO during the race
    respawns the player at the entrance while the race runs on; a reload resumes
    it from its saved running time (see the dispatcher note above). Either way it
    almost always fires: the race is forfeit by design, and Voltage's ink holds the
    after-state (voltage_after_trigger). %>
    {
      "id": "trigger_race",
      "label": "Voltage reaches the laptop in",
      "startOnGlobal": "voltage_fight_started",
      "delayMs": 25000,
